If they continue to eat this much food,

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.818
they could end up weighing up to 

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:24.357
Now, gaining 5 to 10 lb (2.26 to 4.5 kg)

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.826
during the holidays is one thing,

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.696
but gaining 300 lb (136 kg)

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.631
usually happens gradually,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:34.034
after years of bad habits

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.735
combined with other factors.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:39.806
But how about we speed up that process

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.142
and have you gain 300 lb (136 kg) in just one year?

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.077
in just one year?

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.445
What kind of health problems

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.681
could you expect?

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.723
Rapid weight gain is when you put on 

00:00:56.723 --> 00:01:00.293
a large amount of weight in a short time.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.063
And that's what we'll be doing today.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.764
Most people would find it a challenge

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.733
to gain 100 lb (45 kg) in a year.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.702
But we'll be gaining 300 lb (136 kg).

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.241
Could it be eating a mountain

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.210
of McDonald's every day?

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.112
Canceling your gym membership?

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.647
Or both?

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.782
Let's find out.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:26.386
So you're trying to gain 300 lb in a year.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.587
That breaks down to 

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.757
25 lb (11 kg) a month.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.125
There are many factors

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.894
that contribute to rapid weight gain.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.931
Let's start with an obvious one, diet.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.301
One study concluded

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:44.304
that eating 1,000 extra calories a day

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:45.505
for five days

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.308
did not lead to significant weight gain.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.008
However,

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.344
eating 1,000 extra calories a day

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.412
for a month

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.713
led to a weight gain 

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.281
of about 3 lb (1.36 kg) 

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.917
and increased blood sugar.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.220
That's like eating seven or eight 

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.923
Big Macs a day for 30 days.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.792
But those are rookie numbers.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:06.926
To reach your goal 

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.329
of gaining 25 lb (11.3 kg) a month,

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.730
 you would need to quintuple

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.665
that amount of calories.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.467
Wow. That's a lot of Big Macs.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.772
By now, you've gained 25 lb (11.3 kg).

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.441
In addition to eating thousands

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.575
and thousands of calories

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.776
of junk food,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.111
you’ve also incorporated

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.513
a second element

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.114
into your weight gain journey.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:31.951
And that's eliminating exercise. 

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.720
You won't even be able to walk, 

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.788
as that expends too many calories

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.257
for this challenge. 

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:40.160
You may feel a little sluggish,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.361
but the extra weight

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.763
hasn't affected you too much, yet.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.334
Now you've gained 75 lb (34 kg).

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.203
You've begun to notice it, 

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:53.740
both in how you feel and look.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.141
A third and unexpected

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.043
contributor to weight gain

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.745
is lack of sleep.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.748
We burn calories while we sleep.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.417
So to stay on track with our weight gain,

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.919
you're going to need to sleep

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.454
the bare minimum a human needs.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.422
Leading you to feel 

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.424
more and more exhausted. 

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.294
Now you're feeling it.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.330
With 150 extra pounds (68 kg), 

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.731
how could you not?

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.334
You're tired all the time.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.036
You don't recognize yourself.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.304
And you're on the path

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.607
to some serious health problems.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.008
You know, a fourth element

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.977
that plays a role in rapid weight gain

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.580
is genetics.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.647
If you want to complete 

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:35.748
this challenge in time,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.718
 your genetics will have to be pretty bad.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:39.986
At least when it comes

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.422
to keeping your weight off.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:43.089
According to 

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.457
the Harvard Medical School,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.126
more than 400 different genes

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.796
can contribute to obesity.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.598
These genes can affect things like

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:55.501
appetite, metabolism, and feeling full.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.071
So not only are you always craving

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.906
large quantities of food

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.441
that are high in trans fats, 

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.142
carbs, and sugar,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.212
 but your stomach is a bottomless pit

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.481
and your metabolism can't keep up. 

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.918
Over 12 months, you managed

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.020
to combine all the factors,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.990
 eating tons of junk food, not exercising,

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.691
not sleeping enough

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.326
and bad genetics.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.730
And you met your 300 lb (136 kg) goal.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.765
Now what?

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.034
Well, putting on that much weight

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.870
would make it hard to move or walk.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.905
Your bones would have

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.874
trouble supporting you.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.609
You'd likely be diagnosed

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.645
with some significant health problems

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:42.448
 like heart disease, diabetes, or cancer.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.285
Even breathing can become difficult.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.654
Plus, obesity is linked

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.689
to depression and low self-esteem.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.291
So you'd not only be

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.659
physically unhealthy 

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:56.095
but possibly mentally unhealthy as well.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.063
That doesn't sound like

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.299
much of a life at all.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.167
In general,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.702
gaining a large amount of weight

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.737
in a short amount of time

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.173
 is not a healthy or safe thing to do

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.642
and is therefore not worth it.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.544
But if you want to gain weight

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.645
in a healthy way

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.647
by, say, using weight training

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.783
to build muscle slowly over time,

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.152
then yeah, give it a try.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.721
But you won't gain 300 lb (136 kg)

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.289
in a year this way.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.224
And that's a good thing.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.826
You may be game to gain

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:29.228
300 lb (136 kg) in one year,

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.164
 but we don't recommend it.

